<main class="qr-help"><p class="qr-kicker">QR Creator guide</p><h1>Make QR codes that scan reliably</h1><section class="qr-card"><h2>Supported content</h2><p>Create static QR codes for websites, plain text, email, phone calls, SMS, Wi-Fi, contact cards, geographic locations, and calendar events.</p><h2>PNG or SVG?</h2><p>PNG is convenient for documents and social posts. SVG stays crisp at any size and is usually best for professional printing.</p><h2>Contrast and logos</h2><p>Use a dark foreground on a light background. Logos cover some QR modules, so keep them small; the creator automatically uses high error correction when a logo is present.</p><h2>Test before printing</h2><p>Test the final downloaded file with several phones and QR readers at the intended print size. Leave clear space around the code.</p><h2>Static means permanent</h2><p>A static QR code contains the destination itself. Its content cannot be changed after printing; create and print a new code to change it.</p><h2>Privacy</h2><p>Generation is fully client-side. HelloTasks does not send or store your QR content or uploaded logo. Closing or refreshing the page clears it.</p></section></main></div>
